<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00546">
	<title>Intelligent Speed Limit Assist malfunction</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e04100">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e04101">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV055180L.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e04102"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e04103">
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol outputclass="c0586">Check driver assistance system.</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>When Intelligent Speed Limit Assist is not working properly, the warning message will appear on the cluster for several seconds, and the Master warning light (<image href="../../images/WKIA_040.eps" align="left" placement="inline" outputclass="nolabel" scale="15" id="e04104"/>) and speed limit indicator (<image href="../../images/WKIA_082.eps" align="left" placement="inline" outputclass="nolabel" scale="15" id="e04105"/>) will appear on the cluster.</p>
		<p outputclass="across">If this occurs, have your vehicle inspected by a professional workshop. Kia recommends visiting an authorized Kia dealer or service partner.</p>
	</conbody>
</concept>